Subject: [PATCH 18/39] tei-v7 prompt-01: Repository reconnaissance and
 dependency tracing

---
 tei/candidates.jsonl           | 1 +
 trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tei/candidates.jsonl b/tei/candidates.jsonl
index bc7a9e7..2343774 100644
--- a/tei/candidates.jsonl
+++ b/tei/candidates.jsonl
@@ -27,3 +27,4 @@
 {"version_id": "struct-27", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Add an adversarial compatibility checklist to the implementation protocol", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "target_alignment", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"", "replace": "TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + \"\"\"\nBefore finalizing a framework or scientific-library patch, explicitly compare old and new behavior for omitted arguments, null and empty values, boundaries, subclasses, alternate implementations, exception type/message, ordering, mutability, and numerical precision. Add focused tests for changed rows and run representative unchanged rows.\n\""}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.87, "reasoning_soundness": 0.84, "execution_accuracy": 0.82, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.855, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.26}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.24}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 3x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.02, "why": "The compatibility checklist covers omitted values, boundaries, subclasses, exceptions, ordering, and mutability, improving regression awareness and output discipline; it is less useful for discovering the correct repository implementation and is visibly truncated."}
 {"version_id": "struct-28", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Make patch-selection judgments evidence-first and failure-type-aware", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "def build_system_prompt(candidate_length: int) -> str:\n    init_prompt = f\"\"\"\\", "replace": "def build_system_prompt(candidate_length: int) -> str:\n    candidate_length = max(1, min(candidate_length, 32))\n    init_prompt = f\"\"\"\\"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.84, "execution_accuracy": 0.8, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8425, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.23}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.2}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0075, "why": "Evidence-first, failure-type-aware patch selection can modestly improve judgment, but it is primarily a selection-layer change rather than a repository diagnosis or debugging intervention. The bounded candidate length also risks omitting useful prompt guidance, so gains are smaller than the direct protocol changes."}
 {"version_id": "struct-29", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Normalize candidate patch text before judging it", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "        self.patch = patch if isinstance(patch, str) else \"\"", "replace": "        self.patch = patch if isinstance(patch, str) else \"\"\n        self.patch = re.sub(r\"^```(?:diff|patch)?\\s*|\\s*```$\", \"\", self.patch.strip(), flags=re.IGNORECASE)"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.82, "execution_accuracy": 0.79, "output_integrity": 0.93}, "aggregate": 0.85, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.22}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.18}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.015, "why": "Type normalization, trimming, and removal of Markdown fences reduce malformed patch outputs and substantially improve output integrity, but they do not improve diagnosis, implementation, or validation and can potentially alter intentionally formatted patch text."}
+{"version_id": "struct-30", "phase": "structural", "technique": "Strengthen the success gate against placeholder or non-patch outputs", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "evaluation/patch_selection/trae_selector/selector_agent.py", "find": "        self.is_success_patch = bool(is_success_patch and self.cleaned_patch and self.has_patch_content)", "replace": "        self.is_success_patch = bool(\n            is_success_patch\n            and self.has_patch_content\n            and not re.fullmatch(r\"(?is)(?:diff\\s+--git|---|\\+\\+\\+|no\\s+changes?)\\s*\", self.cleaned_patch)\n        )"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.82, "execution_accuracy": 0.8, "output_integrity": 0.95}, "aggregate": 0.8575, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.22}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.18}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0225, "why": "The strengthened success gate blocks placeholder and non-patch text from being accepted, giving the best output-integrity improvement and a slight execution benefit by preventing false positives. It does not help solve the underlying hard repository tasks and may reject edge-case outputs that contain minimal but meaningful diff markers."}
diff --git a/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py b/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py
index 835e701..9c2085f 100644
--- a/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py
+++ b/trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ from trae_agent.prompt.agent_prompt import TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT
 
 TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + """
 
-For framework and scientific-library changes, build a behavior matrix before editing: normal inputs; empty and null inputs; minimum, maximum, and boundary values; subclasses and alternate implementations; omitted versus explicit defaults; expected exceptions and messages; and interactions with existing public APIs. For every row, state whether behavior must remain unchanged or intentionally change, then add or run a focused regression test for each affected row while preserving unrelated behavior. Before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering public API signatures, exception types and messages, ordering, mutability, numerical precision, serialization, subclass behavior, and interactions with neighboring features; reject any change lacking evidence for intentional behavior differences.
+Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, first perform repository reconnaissance: locate the primary implementation, all callers, related subclasses or alternate backends, existing regression tests, and analogous behavior elsewhere in the repository. Trace the relevant data and control flow, state the likely root cause, and identify the smallest compatible change. Then build a behavior matrix before editing: normal inputs; empty and null inputs; minimum, maximum, and boundary values; subclasses and alternate implementations; omitted versus explicit defaults; expected exceptions and messages; and interactions with existing public APIs. For every row, state whether behavior must remain unchanged or intentionally change, then add or run a focused regression test for each affected row while preserving unrelated behavior. Before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering public API signatures, exception types and messages, ordering, mutability, numerical precision, serialization, subclass behavior, and interactions with neighboring features; reject any change lacking evidence for intentional behavior differences.
 """
 
 TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT = TRAE_AGENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT + """
